        "about-pure-titanium": {
          "type": "_faq-category",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "About Pure Titanium",
            "heading_color": "#bca588",
            "icon": "plus",
            "dividers": true,
            "type_preset": "h6"
          },
          "blocks": {
            "row-1": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What is titanium & why does it matter for my safety?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Titanium is simply one of the strongest, non-toxic and most biocompatible metals on Earth. Want the full breakdown of titanium’s science and unique benefits? Read more on our Science Page</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-2": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Why titanium instead of wood, plastic or non-stick?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Because every other option comes with long-term health risks. Plastics shed hormone-disrupting microplastics, wood is full of germs & bacteria that impact your gut, Steel leaches heavy metals, and non-stick coatings release cancer causing PFAS “forever chemicals.” Where’s Titanium: No forever chemicals, no microplastics, no germs. The cleanest, safest & most hygienic surface for cooking & prepping. Resistant to corrosion & lasts a lifetime. 100% recyclable & made for long-term use, reducing waste.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-3": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Is titanium safe for food contact?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes. Titanium never leaches, corrodes, or reacts with your food, at any temperature. It’s so safe that surgeons trust it inside the human body as implants to last a lifetime.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-4": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Is titanium completely toxin-free?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes. Pure titanium is 100% toxin-free. It never leaches, reacts, or contaminates your food - no matter the heat. Unlike other metals, it contains no harmful additives like nickel, chromium, or aluminum, and it’s FDA-compliant for food contact, proven free from extractable lead and other contaminants. With Taima®, you always know what’s touching your food is completely safe.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-5": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Titanium antibacterial properties explained",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes - naturally. Its dense, non-porous surface gives bacteria nowhere to hide. With our advanced Tita-Nano™ surface texture, it even disrupts bacteria on contact, making titanium the most hygienic surface in your kitchen.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-6": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What does “biocompatible” mean?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Pure titanium is the most biocompatible metal on Earth, which is why it’s trusted in devices placed directly inside the human body. Biocompatibility means your body doesn’t react negatively to it. It’s stable, non-reactive, and safe to come into contact with your food every single day. Unlike other materials, it won’t leach heavy metals.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-7": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Does it have heavy metals? Does it corrode?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>No. Pure titanium is the most corrosion-resistant metal in the world. Unlike cast iron, carbon steel, or steel, it never rusts and never reacts with acidic foods. That means no chromium, nickel, or other heavy metals leaching into your meals - ever.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-8": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How long do Taima pure titanium products last?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Unlike wood, plastic, or coated cookware, pure titanium products don’t degrade with time. They can last for decades, making them a perfect one-time investment.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-9": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Are titanium products dishwasher safe?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Absolutely. Unlike non-stick coated pans or wood & plastic boards All of our pure titanium products are dishwasher safe & highly resistant to heat, water, and detergents.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
