        "regular-cookware": {
          "type": "_faq-category",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Regular Cookware",
            "heading_color": "#bca588",
            "icon": "plus",
            "dividers": true,
            "type_preset": "h6"
          },
          "blocks": {
            "row-1": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Downsides of non-stick coated pans",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>The most toxic pan surface there is. Teflon / majority of non-stick pans release toxic PFAS chemicals, known as \"forever chemicals\" which have been linked to cancer and liver damage. The coating easily shaves off over time and can’t handle the heat exposing your food to toxins.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-2": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Downsides of stainless steel pans",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Requires lots of oil to prevent sticking, and reacts with acidic foods - altering taste and leaching heavy metals (nickel, chromium). Tougher to clean, high effort to maintain.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-3": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Downsides of ceramic pans",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Ceramic coatings are very fragile, once chipped, they expose toxic aluminum base. Most only last 1-2 years before losing their non-stick. Expensive to replace, unreliable long-term.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-4": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Downsides of cast iron pans",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Incredibly heavy and high-maintenance - cast iron rusts easily without regular seasoning and struggles with acidic foods, which can degrade the surface and alter flavor.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-5": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How does titanium compare to regular cookware?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Pure titanium never leaches chemicals or heavy metals, resists corrosion completely, and is engineered with our SlipScale™ non-stick surface - giving you the release of coated pans without the toxins, and the durability of steel without the weight or maintenance.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "row-1",
            "row-2",
            "row-3",
            "row-4",
            "row-5"
          ]
        },
        "titanium-cookware": {
          "type": "_faq-category",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Pure Titanium Cookware",
            "heading_color": "#bca588",
            "icon": "plus",
            "dividers": true,
            "type_preset": "h6"
          },
          "blocks": {
            "row-1": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How does SlipScale™ non-stick surface work?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>This technology is the very first of its kind, setting a new standard in cookware. SlipScale™ is our engineered, no-coating imprinted surface pattern that increases food release by up to 3x. The micro-ridges minimize contact points and help distribute oil evenly inside, creating a layer between food & the pan, so food glides off, not sticks.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-2": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How does titanium cookware help food retain more nutrients?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Pure Titanium’s superior thermal conductivity allows you to cook evenly at lower temperatures. Studies show that lower-temp cooking helps retain up to 30% more nutrients (especially vitamin C) in your food compared to traditional cookware.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-3": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What studies show that Pure Titanium cookware retains more nutrients?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>A study published in the Journal of Food Science and Technology investigated how different cookware materials affect nutrient retention. The research revealed that titanium cookware offers the best protection of micronutrients, far outperforming other materials like stainless steel.This superior nutrient retention is attributed to titanium's excellent heat conductivity, which allows for cooking at lower temperatures. Lower cooking temperatures help preserve essential vitamins and minerals that are often lost during high-heat cooking methods.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-4": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Why should I switch from my existing pan?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Because no other pan protects your health, keeps nutrients intact, and lasts for decades like this one.Health: Unlike non-stick, stainless, or ceramic coatings, titanium never leaches chemicals or metals. It’s completely toxin-free.Nutrients: Cooking at lower heat on titanium preserves up to 30% more nutrients. Your food doesn’t just taste better - it’s healthier.Longevity: Traditional pans warp, chip, or lose their coatings. A Taima® titanium pan will outlast them all.Ease of use: Lightweight, versatile, oven-safe, and compatible with every cooktop.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-5": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Is titanium safe for food contact?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes. Titanium never leaches, corrodes, or reacts with your food, at any temperature. It’s so safe that surgeons trust it inside the human body as implants to last a lifetime.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-6": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Why do acidic foods cause problems in other pans?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Acids from pepper, lemon or tomato can react with steel or non-stick coatings, breaking them down and causing heavy metals or chemicals to leach into your food. Titanium is the most corrosion-resistant metal on Earth, so it stays completely stable, no matter what you’re cooking.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-7": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Is it safe to use on all stovetops and ovens?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes. The Taima® Titanium cookware works on every cooking surface - gas, electric, ceramic, induction, open flame & oven. No limitations.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
