            },
            "row-8": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Can I cook at very high temperatures with titanium?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Absolutely. Pure titanium can withstand extreme heat without warping, breaking down, or releasing anything harmful. Just use oil with the right smoke point for your recipe, and you can safely cook at any temperature.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-9": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Does titanium discolor with heat?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes, pure titanium can show color changes when exposed to very high heat (from light brown to blue to rainbow). This isn’t damage, it’s proof of purity. The discoloration is only cosmetic and doesn’t affect performance, safety, or durability.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-10": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Do I need to hand wash or can I use the dishwasher?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Unlike coated pans that get ruined in dishwashers, pure titanium doesn’t care. It’s non-porous, doesn’t absorb grease, odors, or detergent, and won’t degrade. Hand wash or dishwasher - both are completely safe.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-11": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How hot do my pans need to be to start cooking?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Titanium heats evenly and fast, so you don’t need high heat. Low to medium is enough for most meals, saving nutrients and preventing food from sticking. Reserve high heat for searing - the pan can handle it.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text-1"
              ]
            },
            "row-12": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Do I need butter, oil, or cooking spray when cooking?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text-1": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>With our SlipScale™ non-stick surface, you’ll use far less oil than with traditional pans. A touch of butter or oil enhances flavor, but food won’t bond to the surface the way it does with stainless or cast iron.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
